00:35.260 --> 00:38.720
Paris. The end of the 19th century.
Beneath the glass ceiling of the Galerie du Roy,
one can see the thin silhouette of a Japanese girl named Yune.
For now, only a few Parisians know of her arrival...

00:35.260 --> 00:38.720
The crossing in a foreign maze

00:38.720 --> 00:44.100
As I open the gate and step out into the street

00:44.730 --> 00:48.770
asa no hikari ga mabushii

00:44.730 --> 00:48.770
朝の光が眩しい

00:44.730 --> 00:48.770
I can see the sun shining brightly

00:51.780 --> 00:56.780
doko kara ka nagareru hanauta ni

00:51.780 --> 00:56.780
どこからか流れる鼻歌に

00:51.780 --> 00:56.780
I can hear humming in the distance

00:57.950 --> 01:01.700
kokoro hazumi tokete yuku

00:57.950 --> 01:01.700
心弾み解けてゆく

00:57.950 --> 01:01.700
It moves me and melts my heart

01:04.910 --> 01:10.380
mabuta tojireba ukabu egao

01:04.910 --> 01:10.380
瞼閉じれば浮かぶ笑顔

01:04.910 --> 01:10.380
I can see that smile when I close my eyes

01:11.550 --> 01:16.970
omoidasu tabi ni namida hitotsu

01:11.550 --> 01:16.970
思い出す度に涙ひとつ

01:11.550 --> 01:16.970
It brings me to tears whenever I remember it

01:17.470 --> 01:20.600
te wo hiroge hashiridase

01:17.470 --> 01:20.600
手を広げ 走りだせ

01:17.470 --> 01:20.600
Spread your arms out and take off

01:20.600 --> 01:23.930
hi no ataru toori wo

01:20.600 --> 01:23.930
陽の当たる 通りを

01:20.600 --> 01:23.930
Down the streets where the lights shine

01:23.930 --> 01:30.480
michiyuku hito ni genki ni aisatsu

01:23.930 --> 01:30.480
道行く人に 元気に挨拶

01:23.930 --> 01:30.480
Cheerfully greet people walking down the city streets

01:30.480 --> 01:37.110
atarashii kimochi de shinkokyuu shitara

01:30.480 --> 01:37.110
新しい 気持ちで深呼吸したら

01:30.480 --> 01:37.110
Take a deep breath to refresh yourself

01:37.110 --> 01:45.620
kono sekai wa hora itsudemo kimi no mono

01:37.110 --> 01:45.620
この世界はほら いつでも 君のもの

01:37.110 --> 01:45.620
And this world will always be yours

01:51.000 --> 02:01.010
Episode 05 :

01:51.000 --> 02:01.010
" Lost "

02:08.690 --> 02:12.440
You just came from Japan and you're already working.

02:12.440 --> 02:14.530
You do whatever I say,

02:14.530 --> 02:17.320
clean the place up, and repair any clothes that tear.

02:18.740 --> 02:20.320
But...

02:20.320 --> 02:25.330
could you please stop standing here and staring at me when you're done with everything?

02:32.080 --> 02:35.460
It doesn't matter if you're here or there.

02:35.460 --> 02:37.170
Then, what should I do?

02:38.970 --> 02:40.300
Do you know what this is?

02:40.840 --> 02:42.010
Money?

02:42.430 --> 02:44.720
Marianne, the goddess of freedom.

02:44.720 --> 02:46.850
She's the symbol of this nation.

02:48.850 --> 02:51.230
Marianne... Marianne...

02:51.230 --> 02:52.230
I've remembered it!

02:52.230 --> 02:54.110
That's not what I mean.

02:54.110 --> 02:57.610
You're free to do whatever you like.

02:58.610 --> 03:00.240
I can't!

03:00.240 --> 03:02.870
I don't even know what to do when I'm free.

03:03.370 --> 03:06.870
I always thought that was the easiest thing to do...

03:06.870 --> 03:11.460
Just give Yune some work to do, Claude.

03:11.460 --> 03:13.380
You're so weird.

03:13.880 --> 03:16.630
Fine, go polish the lamps in the store.

03:17.760 --> 03:18.300
Okay!

03:21.050 --> 03:25.550
How can she be so excited to work?

03:25.550 --> 03:28.560
Doesn't she ever want some time to herself?

03:28.560 --> 03:31.310
Japanese people are as one.

03:31.310 --> 03:34.900
She feels uneasy when she's not doing the same things as us.

03:36.650 --> 03:38.530
What a troublesome girl.

04:09.060 --> 04:11.930
We aren't getting any customers...

04:19.570 --> 04:21.150
Welcome!

04:21.150 --> 04:22.900
Are you looking for something?

04:23.700 --> 04:25.070
L-Let me see...

04:25.820 --> 04:29.080
We have very pretty things inside the store, too,

04:29.080 --> 04:30.200
so please take a look.

04:30.200 --> 04:34.670
We have lamps, candlesticks, and even iron signs.

04:34.670 --> 04:36.540
Oh, but you wouldn't need that.

04:36.540 --> 04:37.920
Well, we also have-

04:37.920 --> 04:39.170
I'm fine.

04:48.600 --> 04:52.350
Did I do something wrong?

04:54.480 --> 04:57.860
It's because you were talking with such a huge smile.

04:57.860 --> 05:00.730
If you act all friendly to a stranger,

05:00.730 --> 05:02.610
then they'll obviously get scared.

05:02.610 --> 05:04.240
If you're shopkeeping,

05:04.240 --> 05:07.870
you just have to look out for suspicious customers.

05:07.870 --> 05:09.370
What?!

05:09.370 --> 05:10.990
We aren't the only ones.

05:10.990 --> 05:14.120
Be cautious if someone starts acting overly friendly to you.

05:14.120 --> 05:18.210
People who are smiling the entire time are clearly suspicious.

05:18.880 --> 05:24.050
Just because you're getting used to the city doesn't mean you aren't in danger.

05:28.590 --> 05:29.800
That boy...

05:29.800 --> 05:32.220
I think I've seen him before.

05:42.320 --> 05:44.690
Were you even listening to what I said?

05:44.690 --> 05:47.570
You're doing exactly what I told you <i>not</i> to do.

05:47.570 --> 05:49.950
But he's just a small child.

05:49.950 --> 05:52.280
Age doesn't matter!

05:52.280 --> 05:56.210
You need to be especially careful around dirty kids like him.

05:57.040 --> 05:59.580
You're segregating customers by how they look?!

05:59.580 --> 06:01.790
I only told you to be cautious.

06:01.790 --> 06:04.210
The lowest class can't even afford bread.

06:04.800 --> 06:06.970
They have to steal just to live.

06:06.970 --> 06:07.840
But-

06:07.840 --> 06:09.550
You're too naive.

06:11.220 --> 06:14.720
Don't you value your customers, Claude-sama?

06:14.720 --> 06:17.140
I value <i>you</i> even more.

06:22.770 --> 06:24.150
I don't understand.

06:25.780 --> 06:28.450
Everything here is the exact opposite of Japan.

06:28.450 --> 06:32.660
I value customers more than anything else.

06:32.660 --> 06:34.790
I want them to be happy.

06:34.790 --> 06:39.290
I came here to study since I love Paris.

06:39.290 --> 06:43.290
Everybody here, including you, are my teachers.

06:44.550 --> 06:47.800
I want to thank them all for teaching me.

06:47.800 --> 06:48.800
I want to be of use.

06:49.680 --> 06:53.800
But, I can't.

06:53.800 --> 06:56.930
I understand how you feel, Yune,

06:56.930 --> 06:58.810
but we have our own ways here.

06:59.520 --> 07:01.730
You can just sit down.

07:01.730 --> 07:03.560
Tell me if anything happens.

07:04.190 --> 07:05.070
Okay.

07:26.420 --> 07:28.420
I still don't understand.

07:28.420 --> 07:32.840
Can nobody have sympathy for others here?

07:33.640 --> 07:35.220
Oscar-sama.

07:39.140 --> 07:42.850
Ah, the wick is old, so this is useless.

07:43.440 --> 07:47.440
Candles and oil have been replaced by gas,

07:47.440 --> 07:49.820
and the age of electricity will soon come.

07:49.820 --> 07:54.570
When that time comes, oil lamps will become completely useless.

07:56.330 --> 07:59.080
It's just like me.

07:59.830 --> 08:01.710
What are you saying?

08:01.710 --> 08:09.090
You're probably the only one who can clean these lamps so efficiently.

08:10.340 --> 08:12.130
Thank you.

08:14.930 --> 08:21.270
But, you know, some things are left behind in the flow of time,

08:21.270 --> 08:25.020
just like our candlesticks and this <i>Galerie</i>.

08:25.020 --> 08:27.770
Claude-sama said that he wanted to preserve it.

08:27.770 --> 08:31.030
He has his own way of thinking.

08:32.190 --> 08:33.400
Now, then...

08:33.990 --> 08:36.990
What is that luggage for, Oscar-sama?

08:36.990 --> 08:39.330
I got the urge to go on a trip.

08:39.990 --> 08:43.500
But you just came back from Japan!

08:43.500 --> 08:44.330
Leave him alone.

08:45.580 --> 08:47.460
He always does this.

08:47.460 --> 08:48.960
Claude-sama?

08:53.670 --> 08:55.720
What's wrong?

08:55.720 --> 08:59.680
You work so hard to keep the store going,

08:59.680 --> 09:05.810
but does Oscar-sama not care about the shop or the <i>Galerie</i> as much?

09:05.810 --> 09:09.520
Don't mind me. Just let him be himself.

09:21.830 --> 09:24.830
Freedom in Paris is different from freedom in Japan.

09:24.830 --> 09:29.170
Am I not allowed to meddle when I'm free?

09:35.840 --> 09:38.720
Did you want to see something?

09:41.850 --> 09:42.720
That?

10:00.700 --> 10:01.870
Wait!

10:02.660 --> 10:03.580
Yune?

10:21.600 --> 10:22.600
Give that back!

10:26.480 --> 10:27.480
What should I do?

10:27.480 --> 10:28.890
It's all my fault!

10:41.780 --> 10:43.200
I lost him...

10:52.000 --> 10:53.500
I hate the rain.

10:53.500 --> 10:54.750
My dress is ruined now.

10:56.710 --> 10:58.470
Have you seen Yune?

10:58.470 --> 10:59.510
Nope.

10:59.510 --> 11:00.340
I see.

11:02.890 --> 11:03.890
Did she run away?

11:15.020 --> 11:15.690
Um-

11:15.690 --> 11:17.440
That was terrible.

11:17.440 --> 11:19.070
It'll probably stop if we wait it out.

11:21.740 --> 11:24.580
Excuse me-

11:22.320 --> 11:24.580
Look! What a pretty parasol!

11:24.580 --> 11:27.200
You can just buy one at the department store.

11:33.040 --> 11:35.670
Have you see a little boy around here?

11:37.420 --> 11:40.300
Please come in if you like.

11:40.300 --> 11:42.050
The rain probably won't stop for a while.

11:42.680 --> 11:44.140
You're right.

11:45.680 --> 11:49.100
I need to go back and tell Claude-sama.

11:59.860 --> 12:02.860
Claude-sama's shop is...

12:10.080 --> 12:11.580
If I go outside...

12:13.830 --> 12:16.080
Damn it.

12:29.930 --> 12:31.930
Oh no...

12:42.110 --> 12:43.610
I see.

12:43.610 --> 12:45.360
If that's what you're looking for, we have the perfect thing-

12:45.360 --> 12:47.320
Hey, have you see Yune around?

12:47.320 --> 12:48.950
No, I haven't.

12:48.950 --> 12:50.410
All right.

12:50.410 --> 12:52.040
Let me know if you do!

12:52.040 --> 12:53.910
Will do!

12:53.910 --> 12:55.170
Sorry about that.

13:17.020 --> 13:18.020
Look! It's so cool!

13:28.820 --> 13:31.700
There are so many people,

13:31.700 --> 13:34.250
but I can't talk to any of them.

13:47.760 --> 13:49.050
I finally found you,

13:52.180 --> 13:53.140
<i>Japonaise</i>-san.

13:55.230 --> 13:59.480
People who are smiling the entire time are clearly suspicious.

14:01.360 --> 14:02.070
Um-

14:02.070 --> 14:03.940
Are you lost?

14:03.940 --> 14:07.450
The stores in the <i>Galerie</i> all look alike.

14:07.450 --> 14:08.910
Come over here.

14:09.910 --> 14:10.870
Let go!

14:22.710 --> 14:24.380
Where am I?

14:54.910 --> 14:57.910
You shouldn't go so far away on your own.

14:57.910 --> 15:00.290
Although, I guess I <i>did</i> tell you to be free.

15:01.920 --> 15:03.670
Claude-sama...

15:07.010 --> 15:08.260
I'm sorry!

15:09.300 --> 15:11.800
One of our items was stolen.

15:13.550 --> 15:15.560
It's all my fault.

15:15.560 --> 15:18.060
It's because I wasn't cautious enough!

15:19.520 --> 15:20.520
It's fine.

15:20.520 --> 15:26.650
It was a precious item that you, your father, and Oscar-sama made!

15:26.650 --> 15:27.860
Yune,

15:29.320 --> 15:34.200
nothing in the shop is more valuable than your safety.

15:39.660 --> 15:43.460
Thank you...

15:55.720 --> 15:57.600
Do Parisians scare you?

15:59.680 --> 16:04.100
Yes, I should've listened to what you told me.

16:06.730 --> 16:08.360
Don't misunderstand.

16:08.360 --> 16:12.110
I'm not telling you that everyone in Paris is dangerous.

16:12.110 --> 16:13.200
Am I dangerous?

16:13.200 --> 16:14.990
No!

16:14.990 --> 16:19.490
Only one thing separates dangerous people and safe people:

16:19.490 --> 16:22.870
whether they know you or not.

16:22.870 --> 16:26.170
If they think you're a good person,

16:26.170 --> 16:28.880
they will all smile back at you.

16:29.380 --> 16:33.510
Well, it isn't that easy to make friends,

16:33.510 --> 16:37.010
but the people here are pretty cautious.

16:37.010 --> 16:40.640
On the contrary, once they consider you a friend,

16:40.640 --> 16:42.390
they'll care about you for their entire life.

16:42.890 --> 16:45.770
Nothing can change that.

16:45.770 --> 16:47.400
That's how we are.

16:49.020 --> 16:50.360
Okay!

17:14.300 --> 17:17.050
I see. That's worrisome.

17:18.680 --> 17:20.560
You found her, Claude?

17:20.560 --> 17:22.180
Yeah, thanks.

17:22.180 --> 17:24.180
Sorry for worrying you.

17:26.060 --> 17:27.650
Sorry about that.

17:27.650 --> 17:29.770
I didn't mean to startle you.

17:31.070 --> 17:33.150
Was I really that scary?

17:33.150 --> 17:35.070
N-No, you weren't...

17:35.070 --> 17:36.150
What is it?

17:36.150 --> 17:37.280
Um-

17:37.280 --> 17:40.030
When I talked to her when she was lost,

17:40.030 --> 17:43.580
she shook my hand off and ran away as fast as she could.

17:44.450 --> 17:47.790
I see. So you did what I told you to.

17:49.000 --> 17:51.590
I'm sorry!

17:52.050 --> 17:53.760
You were a kind person,

17:53.760 --> 17:56.220
but I thought you were suspicious-looking, so...

17:56.220 --> 17:56.840
I'm sorry!

17:56.970 --> 17:57.590
I'm sorry!

18:01.760 --> 18:02.970
I'm Alan.

18:02.970 --> 18:03.850
Nice to meet you.

18:09.020 --> 18:11.310
Nice to meet you, too.

18:15.610 --> 18:20.990
I presumed that when I smiled, people would smile back,

18:20.990 --> 18:29.040
but when I learned that wasn't the case, I thought everyone in Paris was dangerous.

18:29.040 --> 18:33.170
I took my own freedom away.

18:33.170 --> 18:36.170
Then I'm not free, either.

18:36.170 --> 18:38.170
No, you're-

18:39.180 --> 18:40.800
Look.

18:42.260 --> 18:43.930
<i>Enseignes du Roy.</i>

18:44.390 --> 18:47.140
Remember what that sign looks like.

18:47.140 --> 18:49.690
Yes, Claude-sama.

18:51.270 --> 18:53.690
<i>I can't lose this.</i>

18:53.690 --> 18:58.150
<i>His back is my precious...</i>

19:16.500 --> 19:17.710
I'm home.

19:17.710 --> 19:19.090
Oscar-sama!

19:19.090 --> 19:22.430
Don't expect any dinner. I didn't make you any.

19:22.970 --> 19:26.100
Weren't you on a trip, Oscar-sama?

19:26.100 --> 19:29.230
Well, I was worried about you,

19:29.230 --> 19:31.480
so I decided to stay in Paris for a little longer.

19:31.480 --> 19:35.230
Did you find a lover from before around here?

19:36.150 --> 19:40.740
Bring me one of the lamps you polished today, Yune.

19:43.450 --> 19:45.660
If you change the wick,

19:45.660 --> 19:48.290
you can use it again.

19:56.040 --> 19:59.170
You're just like this lamp, right?

19:59.170 --> 20:00.130
Yes.

20:00.130 --> 20:01.050
What do you mean?

20:01.670 --> 20:06.260
You came to a dull, boring home with only men,

20:06.260 --> 20:09.720
and gave us a warm light.

20:11.270 --> 20:14.060
No, that isn't-

20:14.060 --> 20:20.820
So, even if I go on a date, you shouldn't be bored.

20:21.440 --> 20:24.320
Take good care of Claude, Yune.

20:25.660 --> 20:26.200
Bye.

20:28.370 --> 20:29.870
I'll be back by morning.

20:31.200 --> 20:32.620
Yep, it's a lover.

20:36.210 --> 20:37.960
Please forgive him.

20:38.590 --> 20:40.960
He's always been like that,

20:40.960 --> 20:43.800
but he's the wonderful man who
founded <i>Enseignes du Roy</i>.

20:44.590 --> 20:48.850
The least I can do for him is to protect the store,

20:48.850 --> 20:51.850
and yet, I'm a small-minded man who can barely manage to do that.

20:53.640 --> 20:59.270
I don't care if he's out enjoying life, as long as he's happy.

21:00.360 --> 21:04.320
I'm sorry, I was presuming things again.

21:04.320 --> 21:08.580
I was also being small-minded.

21:08.580 --> 21:10.540
You <i>are</i> still small.

21:10.540 --> 21:12.950
I'm not talking about my size!

21:36.020 --> 21:42.610
aa marude yume wo miteru you na

21:36.020 --> 21:42.610
ああ、まるで夢を見てるような

21:36.020 --> 21:42.610
Ah, it's as if I'm in a dream

21:42.610 --> 21:48.410
yawarakana hikari no naka de

21:42.610 --> 21:48.410
柔らかな光の中で

21:42.610 --> 21:48.410
As I lie here in this tender light

21:48.410 --> 21:59.420
me wo tojite mimi wo sumasereba kikoete kuru

21:48.410 --> 21:59.420
目を閉じて耳を澄ませれば　聞こえてくる

21:48.410 --> 21:59.420
When I close my eyes and listen, I can hear it

22:01.250 --> 22:14.310
atatakaku watashi wo yobu yasashii sono koe ga

22:01.250 --> 22:14.310
あたたかく私を呼ぶ優しいその声が

22:01.250 --> 22:14.310
That kind voice that warmly calls to me

22:16.890 --> 22:23.480
afureru omoi wo tsutaetai kono te kara

22:16.890 --> 22:23.480
溢れる思いを伝えたい　この手から

22:16.890 --> 22:23.480
I want to extend my feelings with these hands

22:23.480 --> 22:29.780
kotoba ja nakute kokoro de tsunagaru

22:23.480 --> 22:29.780
言葉じゃなくて　心で繋がる

22:23.480 --> 22:29.780
We connect through our hearts, not our words

22:29.780 --> 22:36.450
hajimeyou koko kara sodateyou nukumori wo

22:29.780 --> 22:36.450
始めよう　ここから育てよう　温もりを

22:29.780 --> 22:36.450
Let's begin here. Let's nurture the warmth

22:36.450 --> 22:42.920
atarashii hibi ga watashi wo matteru

22:36.450 --> 22:42.920
新しい日々が私を待ってる

22:36.450 --> 22:42.920
A new day is waiting for me

22:42.920 --> 22:56.640
mamoru mono wa kitto koko ni aru no

22:42.920 --> 22:56.640
守るものはきっとここにあるの

22:42.920 --> 22:56.640
I'm sure there is something here for me to protect

23:35.180 --> 23:36.350
Next episode:

23:36.430 --> 24:36.570
Episode 06 :

23:36.430 --> 24:36.570
" Crinoline "

23:37.680 --> 23:38.600
